WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.684 --> 00:00:10.584
The White House Accord on Super Intelligence is short. About 300 words, on a single page.

2
00:00:11.151 --> 00:00:16.904
For companies building the most advanced SI models, it describes four layers of checks.

3
00:00:17.284 --> 00:00:24.744
One. Internal controls that track what a model can do, including cyber, biological and chemical risks.

4
00:00:25.044 --> 00:00:31.224
Two. An internal team that makes sure those controls really work, and fixes what doesn't.

5
00:00:31.604 --> 00:00:35.864
Three. An independent outside auditor or evaluator.

6
00:00:36.364 --> 00:00:42.584
Four. A committee of the company's board that receives the reports, and makes sure problems get fixed.

7
00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:46.324
The signers also agree to work together on shared safety

8
00:00:46.324 --> 00:00:47.411
standards.

9
00:00:47.644 --> 00:00:57.464
It was signed by Google, Anthropic, Meta, OpenAI, xAI and Nvidia, and by President Trump, who called it “morally binding.”

10
00:00:57.764 --> 00:01:04.824
But it is voluntary. The text sets no penalties, and it doesn't require results to be made public.

11
00:01:05.044 --> 00:01:13.384
Google's Sundar Pichai called it “a solid basis for moving forward.” The Council on Foreign Relations called it toothless.
